@startuml
' Figure 21-4: SYMBOL-ONCE realized in Rho. The subject App(Lam(body), arg) is spread as a
' flat parallel composition of ground sends — each node publishes its head tag ONCE on its
' deterministic location channel. Because the spread is single-shot linear, each head tag is
' consumed by EXACTLY ONE for-receive (one interned sa:-state), so no symbol is re-inspected.
' The sa: COMMs are internal (tau); only the final rule firing is a visible COMM. The mechanism
' itself is owned by docs 15/20 — this figure shows only the symbol-once accounting (Theorem
' thm:symbol-once, optimal-channels.tex:457).
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName monospaced
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #4A5568
  LifeLineBorderColor #4A5568
  ParticipantBorderColor #4A5568
  ParticipantFontColor #1A202C
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F0FE
  ActorBorderColor #4A5568
}
skinparam ArrowColor #4A5568
title Figure 21-4 — symbol-once in Rho: each spread head tag is consumed by exactly one for-receive\nsubject  App(Lam(body), arg)  reduces to the reduct, sigma = [body, arg]

participant "spread <latex>[\![ t ]\!]</latex>\n(ground sends)" as SUB #EDE7F6
participant "sa: state <latex>s_0</latex>\n<latex>\mathrm{for}(h \Leftarrow c(\epsilon))</latex>" as S0 #C3DAF7
participant "sa: state <latex>s_{app}</latex>\n<latex>\mathrm{for}(h \Leftarrow c(1))</latex>" as SAPP #C3DAF7
participant "<latex>\sigma</latex>-receiver\n(rule channel)" as SIG #B7E4C7
participant "OUT" as OUT #9FD3B4

note over SUB #FCF3D0
  Each node publishes ITS head tag exactly once:
  <latex>c(\epsilon)\,!\,(\mathrm{app})\ \ |\ \ c(1)\,!\,(\mathrm{lam})\ \ |\ \ \ldots</latex>
end note

SUB -[#2B6CB0]->> S0 : <latex>c(\epsilon)\,!\,(\mathrm{app})</latex>
activate S0
note right of S0 #E6F4EA
  <latex>\tau</latex> (internal): match app,
  advance to child 1   <latex>[\,\delta(s_0,\mathrm{app})\,]</latex>
end note
S0 -[#2B6CB0]->> SAPP : advance frontier to position 1
deactivate S0

activate SAPP
SUB -[#805AD5]->> SAPP : <latex>c(1)\,!\,(\mathrm{lam})</latex>
note right of SAPP #E6F4EA
  <latex>\tau</latex> (internal): match lam,
  goal completes   <latex>[\,\eta(s_{app},\mathrm{lam})\,]</latex>
end note
SAPP -[#2F855A]->> SIG : <latex>\mathrm{accept}\,!\,(\sigma),\ \ \sigma=[\mathrm{body},\mathrm{arg}]</latex>
deactivate SAPP

activate SIG
SIG -[#C05621]->> OUT : <latex>[\![ R ]\!]\sigma</latex>   (the single VISIBLE COMM)
deactivate SIG

note over S0, SAPP #FFF5F5
  |= subject symbol |= for-receives that consume it |
  | app | exactly 1  (state s0) |
  | lam | exactly 1  (state s_app) |
  Total surface symbols consumed = total for-receives fired  <latex>\Rightarrow</latex>  O1.
end note
@enduml
